<h2>Complete one article</h2>
<ol class="handoff-steps"><li><strong>Bring your article.</strong> Review the import preview and every conversion notice before applying it. Headings, lists, links, emphasis, and simple tables can be kept. Images become placeholders; complex layouts need work in your destination.</li><li><strong>Read the converted article.</strong> Compare it with the original. In the Word and Google Docs tools, open Edit article text and formatting only if you need changes. The editor uses Markdown. Local checks help find a few writing and formatting issues; they do not verify facts.</li><li><strong>Take it to WordPress.</strong> Check the review box and copy WordPress blocks. Copy the title separately. In a new empty post, use the full post Code editor for the body, return to Visual editor, and inspect every block before publishing yourself. <a href="/help/publishing-handoff/#wordpress">Detailed WordPress steps</a>.</li></ol>
<h2>Keep unfinished work</h2><p>Writing starts in tab memory. Choose optional browser recovery to keep one unencrypted workspace on this browser, or download a private backup file. Check the saved status or actual file before leaving. Browser recovery is off by default, does not sync, and is not guaranteed. <a href="/help/local-workspace/#browser-recovery">Recovery and privacy details</a>.</p>
<h2>Taking part in the alpha?</h2><p>Use a non-sensitive article you have permission to use. Start with a normal article that includes headings, a list, and a link. An article with a table or image can help expose conversion limits. Keep the original.</p>
<ol><li>First try your normal way of moving the article into WordPress. Note the total time and cleanup needed.</li><li>Use Draft to Page with a similar article. Include import, review, image work, and final WordPress cleanup in the time.</li><li>Record anything confusing, omitted, or broken and whether you would use it for your next article.</li><li>Try keeping and reopening a recovery copy with fictional writing. Review again before exporting.</li></ol>
<p><a href="/alpha-test-checklist.md" download>Download the alpha test notes template</a>. This is a file for your own notes. The site does not collect or submit your responses. Share findings through the private route agreed with the owner; keep private writing out of public issues.</p>
